<description>
Recolor the unique safe route between the two maroon endpoints from teal to maroon.

Input structure
- A black background contains a teal 4-connected track, exactly two maroon endpoint pixels, and one or more orange blocker pixels embedded near the track.

Rule
- Treat each orange blocker and its 8-neighborhood as forbidden.
- In the remaining teal/maroon track graph, there is exactly one simple
  4-connected path between the maroon endpoints.
- Recolor teal pixels on that path to maroon; leave endpoints, blockers, and all other cells unchanged.

Key insight
- The orange pixels block nearby teal cells diagonally as well as orthogonally, which removes shorter decoy routes and makes the intended endpoint-to-endpoint path unique.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "two maroon endpoint pixels on the teal track",
  "path": "unique shortest 4-connected route between the endpoints through teal/maroon cells after treating every orange blocker and its 8-neighborhood as forbidden",
  "trajectory": "paint the teal cells on the route maroon",
  "transform": "keep the endpoints, orange blockers, black background, and off-route teal cells unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 7-9 rows x 9 cols, both dimensions odd
  colors: BLACK(0) background, TEAL(8) track, MAROON(9) endpoints, ORANGE(7) blockers
  track:
    structure: 4-connected planar graph forming a lattice/maze (horizontal bars + vertical connectors)
    cells: 26-42 teal+maroon cells total
    connectivity: single connected component, 1-9 independent cycles (not a tree)
    degree: exactly 2 degree-1 nodes (the endpoints); all other nodes degree 2-4
  endpoints:
    count: exactly 2 MAROON cells
    position: each on the grid border (row 0, row H-1, col 0, or col W-1)
    degree: 1 in the track graph (leaf nodes)
  blockers:
    count: 1-2 ORANGE cells
    position: interior to track bounding box, surrounded by track cells (adjacent to 2-4 track cells)
    effect: each blocker + its 8-neighborhood becomes forbidden; blocks 5-8 track cells
  path:
    rule: exactly one simple 4-connected path between endpoints through passable track (track minus forbidden)
    length: 12-20 edges
    turns: 2-8 direction changes
    coverage: path traverses 50-68% of total track cells
    uniqueness: critical - safe simple path count is exactly 1; unique-shortest alone is insufficient
  output: teal cells on the sole safe endpoint-to-endpoint path recolored to maroon; everything else unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: path-first (build lattice, choose path, place blockers to force uniqueness)
  steps:
    - Choose grid size (7x9 or 9x9) and lattice layout: 2-4 horizontal bars spanning 5-8 cols, spaced 2 rows apart, with vertical connectors at subset of columns between adjacent bars
    - Place 2 endpoint stems as degree-1 extensions from lattice edges to the grid border
    - Designate a target path through the lattice (12-20 edges, >=2 turns)
    - Place 1-2 orange blockers at interior lattice positions whose 8-neighborhoods block all but one endpoint-to-endpoint route
    - Validate: count simple paths in the passable graph and require exactly 1; then check path length, turns, and coverage
```
